<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Gabriel Villagrán, his engineering work, learning path, and the people who helped shape it.">
  <header class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">About Gabriel</span><h1>A little about me.</h1><p>I’m Gabriel, a software engineer from Mexico. I started out working with industrial systems and eventually moved into mobile and web development. I’ve learned a lot by working on different kinds of projects, and there’s still plenty I want to get better at.</p></header>
  <div class="content-layout">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>I’ve spent a good part of my career working with Swift and iOS, including cart and checkout features for Sam’s Club. Before that, I worked on mobile and web applications connected to Laravel APIs, and on industrial monitoring systems using SCADA and SQL. The technologies have changed from one job to another, but what I enjoy most is figuring out how a system works and finding ways to make it better.</p>
      <p>I originally wrote some of the articles on this site in 2022, when I was part of LaunchX, a learning program supported by Microsoft. I’ve gone back to update a few of them because I understand those topics better now. I kept the original dates because I like being able to look back and see what I was learning at the time.</p>
      <h2>People I want to thank</h2>
      <p>I also want to mention a few people who helped me when I was studying and starting out: Dr. Pedro David Arjona Villicaña, Dr. José Ignacio Núñez Varela, Fernanda Ochoa, Rodrigo Martínez, and Carlo Gilmar. I learned a lot from them, and I appreciate the time they took to teach me and answer my questions.</p>
      <p>When I’m not coding, I’m usually listening to metal, playing video games, or picking up my guitar to play some rock and heavy metal. I also enjoy watching videos about networking and cybersecurity. I’m currently learning Norwegian, and I’d love to become fluent one day. Oh, and I’m a big fan of Cruz Azul and the Seattle Seahawks.</p>
      <p>Music is a big part of my life. If you're into music too, <a href="https://open.spotify.com/user/12137688570?si=60bcae74be154a7c" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">follow me on Spotify ↗</a>.</p>
      <div class="quote-card"><blockquote>“Don’t let the theory stop you from reaching your goal.”</blockquote><p>I still think about this quote from David Bombal when I get stuck learning something.</p></div>
    </div>
